tions for resilience and blue carbon. Estuarine, Coastal and Shelf Science. 2017;187:216&#x2013;230. doi: 10.1016/j.ecss.2017.01.005.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1016/j.ecss.2017.01.005</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Filzmoser P, Gschwandtner M. mvoutlier: multivariate outlier detection based on robust methods. 2021. https://CRAN.R-project.org/package=mvoutlier https://CRAN.R-project.org/package=mvoutlier R package version 2.1.1.</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>Fourqurean JW, Duarte CM, Kennedy H, Marb&#xe0; N, Holmer M, Mateo MA, Apostolaki ET, Kendrick GA, Krause-Jensen D, McGlathery KJ, Serrano O. Seagrass ecosystems as a globally significant carbon stock. Nature Geoscience. 2012;5(7):505&#x2013;509. doi: 10.1038/ngeo1477.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1038/ngeo1477</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Fox J, Weisberg S. An R companion to applied regression. Third Edition. Thousand Oaks CA: Sage; 2019.</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>Garcias-Bonet N, Duarte CM. Methane production by seagrass ecosystems in the red sea. Frontiers in Marine Science. 2017;4(Nov):141. doi: 10.3389/fmars.2017.00340.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.3389/fmars.2017.00340</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Hemminga MA, Duarte CM. Seagrass ecology. Cambridge, UK: Cambridge University Press; 2000.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1017/CBO9780511525551</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Hothorn T, Bretz F, Westfall P. Simultaneous inference in general parametric models. Biometrical Journal. 2008;50(3):346&#x2013;363.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">18481363</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Ibanez F. pastecs: package for analysis of space-time ecological series. 2018. https://CRAN.R-project.org/package=pastecs https://CRAN.R-project.org/pack