/s41564-019-0363-3</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1038/s41564-019-0363-3</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC6453112</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">30833729</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Des Marais DJ. The Biogeochemistry of Hypersaline Microbial Mats. In: Jones JG, editor. Advances in Microbial Ecology. Boston, MA: Springer US; 1995. pp. 251&#x2013;274. doi: 10.1007/978-1-4684-7724-5_6</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1007/978-1-4684-7724-5_6</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">11539110</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Vogel M, Des Marais D, Parenteau M, Jahnke L, Turk-Kubo K, Kubo M. Biological influences on modern sulfates: Textures and composition of gypsum deposits from Guerrero Negro, Baja California Sur, Mexico. Sediment Geol. 2010;223: 265&#x2013;280. doi: 10.1016/j.sedgeo.2009.11.013</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1016/j.sedgeo.2009.11.013</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Ni S, Boone DR. Isolation and Characterization of a Dimethyl Sulfide-Degrading Methanogen, Methanolobus siciliae HI350, from an Oil Well, Characterization of M. siciliae T4/MT, and Emendation of M. siciliae. IJSEM. 1991;41: 410&#x2013;416. doi: 10.1099/00207713-41-3-410</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1099/00207713-41-3-410</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">1883716</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Garrity G, Boone DR, Castenholz RW, editors. Bergey&#x2019;s Manual of Systematic Bacteriology: Volume One: The Archaea and the Deeply Branching and Phototrophic Bacteria. 2nd ed. New York: Springer-Verlag; 2001. Available: https://www.springer.com/gp/book/9780387987712</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>King GM. Methanogenesis from Methylated Amines in a Hypersaline Algal Mat. Appl Environ Microbiol. 1988;54: 130&#x2013;136. doi: 10.1128/aem.54.1.130-136.1988</Citation><ArticleIdList>