2" MajorTopicYN="N">Phylogeny</DescriptorName></MeshHeading></MeshHeadingList><CoiStatement>The authors declare no conflict of interest.</CoiStatement></MedlineCitation><PubmedData><History><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="received"><Year>2023</Year><Month>10</Month><Day>1</Day></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="accepted"><Year>2024</Year><Month>4</Month><Day>6</Day></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="medline"><Year>2024</Year><Month>5</Month><Day>6</Day><Hour>0</Hour><Minute>53</Minute></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="pubmed"><Year>2024</Year><Month>5</Month><Day>6</Day><Hour>0</Hour><Minute>52</Minute></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="entrez"><Year>2024</Year><Month>5</Month><Day>5</Day><Hour>21</Hour><Minute>53</Minute></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="pmc-release"><Year>2024</Year><Month>5</Month><Day>5</Day></PubMedPubDate></History><PublicationStatus>ppublish</PublicationStatus><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">38705733</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC11070330</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1111/1758-2229.13263</ArticleId></ArticleIdList><ReferenceList><Reference><Citation>Aromokeye, D.A. , Kulkarni, A.C. , Elvert, M. , Wegener, G. , Henkel, S. , Coffinet, S. et al. (2020) Rates and microbial players of iron&#x2010;driven anaerobic oxidation of methane in methanic marine sediments. Frontiers in Microbiology, 1, 3041.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC6979488</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">32010098</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Atwood, T.B. , Witt, A. , Mayorga, J. , Hammill, E. &amp; Sala, E. (2020) Global patterns in marine sediment carbon stocks. Frontiers in Marine Science, 7, 165.</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>

